<title>USA: TECNOL Medical Products Inc Q4 net up.</title>
<headline>TECNOL Medical Products Inc Q4 net up.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>	    Three Months Ended	    Year Ended</p>
<p>	    11/30/96	 12/2/95     11/30/96   12/2/95</p>
<p>Net sales $36,841	  $31,541     $144,393   $120,922</p>
<p>Income before income taxes</p>
<p>		7,127	    5,757	 23,987     20,993</p>
<p>Income taxes</p>
<p>		2,356	    1,609	  7,986	7,205</p>
<p>Net income</p>
<p>	     $4,771	  $ 4,148	$16,001    $13,788</p>
<p>Net income per share</p>
<p>		$0.24	    $0.21	  $0.80	$0.69</p>
<p>Average shares outstanding</p>
<p>	     20,003	   20,153	 20,092     20,123</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said totals for 1996 include significant one-time charges in the third quarter. It did not specify what the charges were.  </p>
<p>Later, Warren Henry, the company's vice president-investor relations, said the charges covered bad debt, obsolete inventory, rebates and a litigation settlement that in total cut earnings by $0.11 per share.</p>
</text>
